      "notes": "exec: labctl exec win98se \"<cmd>\" runs a command through COMMAND.COM in the guest and captures its stdout (exec_kind warpd_e, host client /root/gexec.py, GEXEC_HOST=exec_host). The agent is C:\\WARPNET.EXE (streamhost/guest-agents/win9x/warpnet.c built -DWARP_PORT=7788), binding 0.0.0.0:7788; reached DIRECTLY over the retronet bridge at the guest IP 10.99.0.10:7788 (n0 is a tap on vmbr-rn, NOT slirp — no hostfwd). It is RUNNING inside the golden and restarts from the StartUp folder on a cold boot. No stderr (COMMAND.COM has no 2>&1). NEVER launch a full-screen DOS box: it wedges the display driver until loadvm golden. See docs/lab/retronet/ICQ-STATION.md, EXEC-CHANNEL.md"
